ny limits of indeterminate form 0/0 or infinity/infinity can be resolved with L'Hopital's Rule, which states that if lim(x->c) f(x)/g(x) is of indeterminate form, then it equals lim(x->c) f'(x)/g'(x), provided that second limit exists. Common techniques for evaluating limits include direct substitution when the function is continuous at that point, factoring and cancelling common terms to remove a